Yes. But also no. I feel like cleaning up the data should come after gettin=
g a new jbovlaste thing where people can better input and delete entries an=
d a way to fix the horrible issue of everyone inputting the latex x's diffe=
rently. I had to write a mean long regex to handle all the different creati=
ve ways people have input those latex x's. I don't have a clear vision abou=
t /how/ exactly that kind of interface should look and behave so I haven't =
been working on it.

Definitely I want the way the definitions are internally stored to be split=
 by the x-components. Maybe even this way would allow a dictionary to (more=
 easily) display definitions outside of the cursed x1 selbri xn English ord=
er. Maybe a way to add tags to the internal representation of the x's such =
as 'event' or 'du'u': that would be plixau.

As for the encoding issue, jbovlaste is on github so you have the ability t=
o find the bug yourself if you want. It's good to know that error is there =
though.

